SEL relays: the records in ``settings.json`` and the SELOGIC equations in ``logic-equations.json`` now have a full name, description, allowed values, units, and a security flag. These come from the relay's own settings files first, then from an optional user file (the new ``sel.setting_descriptions_file`` option), then from PEAT's curated, family- and model-aware descriptions and patterns. ``formatted-logic.txt`` also lists the equations with their descriptions, and ``extra.sel_security_settings`` summarizes the enabled network services and access limits.
